    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners` \u2014 it is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerFieldsDto`, optional `Idempotency-Key` header). I've split it into the request\u2011binding phase (which runs before the method body) and the controller body, and marked each step as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side\u2011effect** (mutates the owner/DTO, writes state, or logs).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Security (before anything else)\n\n1. **Validation \u2014 authorization.** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Without the `OWNER_ADMIN` role the request is rejected (403) before the body is touched.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Request-body binding & `@Valid` (before the method body runs)\n\nThese run while Spring resolves the `OwnerFieldsDto` argument. The bean-validation constraints and the two `@InitBinder`-registered validators (`OwnerFieldsValidator`, then `RegistrationDateValidator`) all contribute field errors to the same `Errors`; any error \u2192 400.\n\n2. **Validation \u2014 Bean Validation constraints on the DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto` getters): `firstName` `@NotNull`, letters-only `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`; `lastName` `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`; `city` `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`; `telephone` `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`; `address` `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` `@Size(max 255)`; `email` `@Size(max 255)`. `title` must be one of `MR/MRS/MS/DR`.\n\nThen `OwnerFieldsValidator.validate` runs, in this order:\n\n3. **Side-effect \u2014 address canonicalization.** If `addressLine1` is non-blank, `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` are normalized and written back, and `address` is composed as `line1 [+ \" \" + line2]`. Otherwise the flat `address` is normalized and written back.\n4. **Validation \u2014 address required.** After canonicalization, if `address` is null/blank \u2192 field error on `address`.\n5. **Validation \u2014 required text fields.** `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` rejected if empty/whitespace.\n6. **Side-effect + validation \u2014 telephone.** Only if `telephone` has no prior error: normalize to E.164 and write it back; if it can't be normalized \u2192 field error `telephone.invalid`.\n7. **Validation + side-effect \u2014 email** (only when supplied): must be syntactically valid (`email.invalid`), must not be a disposable domain (`email.disposable`); if valid, it is normalized to lower case and written back.\n8. **Validation \u2014 postcode** (only when supplied): must be valid for the owner's `city` per the fixed region ranges, else `postcode.invalid`.\n\nThen `RegistrationDateValidator.validate`:\n\n9. **Validation \u2014 registration date not in the future.** If a `registrationDate` was supplied and it is after the server's current date \u2192 `registrationDate.future`.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Controller body (`addOwner`), in execution order\n\n10. **Side-effect (short-circuit) \u2014 idempotency replay.** If an `Idempotency-Key` header is present and already known in `IdempotentOwnerStore`, the previously created owner is re-read and returned (200 OK); nothing below runs.\n11. **Side-effect \u2014 map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`): copies the (now canonicalized) fields into a new transient `Owner`.\n12. **Side-effect \u2014 assign registration date** (`RegistrationDateAssigner`): defaults to the server's current date when none supplied, then rolls weekends/public holidays forward to the next business day; writes back the adjusted date.\n13. **Validation \u2014 city capacity** (`CityCapacityChecker`): if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 409 CONFLICT.\n14. **Validation \u2014 daily registration limit** (`DailyRegistrationLimiter`): if \u2265 100 owners already carry this (adjusted) registration date \u2192 429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS.\n15. **Side-effect \u2014 assign household id** (`HouseholdAssigner`): deterministic id derived from normalized last name + postcode; written to the owner.\n16. **Validation \u2014 household duplicate** (`HouseholdDuplicateChecker`): if another owner already shares the household **and** the request did not set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 409 CONFLICT. (When `sharesHousehold=true`, the owner is recorded internally as a *declared household member* for step 22.)\n17. **Validation \u2014 identity duplicate** (`IdentityDuplicateChecker`): if any non-deleted owner has the same identity key (telephone|email|householdId) \u2192 409 CONFLICT.\n18. **Side-effect \u2014 assign household size** (`HouseholdSizeAssigner`): count of stored owners sharing the household + 1 (or 1 if no household).\n19. **Side-effect \u2014 assign customer code** (`CustomerCodeAssigner`): `<REGION>-<HASH8>` from region + SHA-256 of telephone+lastName, de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix against existing codes.\n20. **Side-effect \u2014 assign namesake count** (`NamesakeCounter`): number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n21. **Side-effect \u2014 assign membership points & level** (`MembershipLevelAssigner`): tallies points (email, no namesakes, large household; tenure is always 0 on create) and bands into level 1\u20134.\n22. **Side-effect \u2014 assign bulk-signup warning** (`BulkSignupWarningAssigner`): `true` if > 80 owners already carry this registration date.\n23. **Side-effect \u2014 assign possible-duplicate flag** (`PossibleDuplicateAssigner` / `PossibleDuplicateMatcher`): unless the owner is a declared household member, soft-match (same last name + postcode, different telephone) sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest match's id.\n24. **Side-effect \u2014 persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`): the owner is saved and assigned its id.\n25. **Side-effect \u2014 remember idempotency key** (`IdempotentOwnerStore.remember`): if a key was supplied, store `key \u2192 owner.id`.\n26. **Side-effect \u2014 audit log** (`OwnerCreationAuditLogger.logCreated`): writes one line to the `AUDIT` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n27. **Side-effect \u2014 build response**: map to `OwnerDto`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return 201 CREATED.\n\nA few things worth calling out: the duplicate/identity checks (16\u201317) and all the count-based assigners (13\u201314, 18\u201323) read the *pre-save* store, so they never count the owner itself; deleted owners are excluded from the household and identity checks. Many response fields (`salutation`, `ageBand`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `region`/`locality`/`timezone`, `telephoneDisplay`, `identityKey`) are **not** assigned here \u2014 they're derived on read in the `Owner` model / mapper, so they aren't creation side-effects."
